                     /note="Promoter of the Tn5 neo (nptII) kanamycin-resistance
                     gene: the 50 bp that the Tn5 record U00004 annotates as the
                     aminoglycoside phosphotransferase promoter region
                     (1413-1462, experimental evidence). Rothstein and Reznikoff
                     (1981) found that the one base differing between IS50L and
                     IS50R (U00004 1442, base 30 here) makes a better promoter.
                     The -35, -10 and start are not placed: provisional
                     boundaries. The 120 bp this part carried before were 12 bp
                     of Tn5 upstream of this window (U00004 1401-1412), 57 bp of
                     Tn5 downstream of it (1463-1519), and 51 bp of linker and
                     ribosome binding site that Tn5 does not carry at all."
